    "teach_4": {
      "id": "teach_4",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Now switch from repetition to cancellation.\n\n1/(√3+√2) can be rationalised with √3−√2.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_4_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_4_step": {
      "id": "teach_4_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Because (√3+√2)(√3−√2)=1, we get:\n\n1/(√3+√2) = √3−√2\n\nThis identity is the engine behind telescoping root sums.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_4"
        }
      ]
    },
